# Building a Cloud Center of Excellence

## From Scratch — Azure, AWS & Bare Metal

**Vince Maidens** · August 2026

<!--
Opening slide — set the tone. This is a strategic plan, not a technical deep-dive.
The audience is leadership — focus on outcomes, not tooling.
-->

---

## Core Principles

- **Enable, don't block** — self-service by default, guardrails not gates
- **Measure everything** — FinOps, security posture, adoption velocity
- **Start small, scale fast** — pilot, prove, then expand
- **Hybrid-aware** — bare metal is first-class, not legacy

<!--
These principles guide every decision. The CCoE is an enabler,
not a police force. This is critical for buy-in.
-->

---

## Team Structure (~7-8 FTEs)

| Role | Count | Focus |
|------|-------|-------|
| CCoE Leads | 3 | Strategy, executive reporting (Alan George, Peter Male, Vince Maidens) |
| Cloud Architect | 1-2 | Azure/AWS standards, design reviews |
| FinOps Analyst | 1 | Cost visibility, optimisation |
| Security Lead | 1 | NCSC CSP, IAM, policy |
| Platform Engineer | 1-2 | Landing zones, IaC, automation |
| Developer Advocate | 1 | Training, docs, evangelism |

<!--
Lean team. Some roles can be part-time initially.
The CCoE Lead (Vince) sets strategy; the team executes.
-->

---

## 24-Week Roadmap

| Phase | Weeks | Focus |
|-------|-------|-------|
| **0 — Foundation** | 1-4 | See everything, win fast |
| **1 — Guardrails** | 5-10 | Safe self-service |
| **2 — Enablement** | 11-16 | Accelerate adoption |
| **3 — Optimisation** | 17-24 | Continuous improvement |

<!--
The roadmap is the heart of the plan.
Each phase builds on the last, with quick wins in Phase 0.
-->

---

## Phase 0: Quick Wins (First 30 Days)

1. **Tag compliance report + auto-tag policy** — visibility in 1 day
2. **Rightsize idle VMs** — immediate cost savings in 2 days
3. **Enable Azure Policy baseline** — NCSC CSP aligned in 1 day
4. **Publish Cloud Playbook** — how to deploy a web app
5. **Set up cost alerts** — subscription-level governance
6. **Bare metal risk register** — top 10 highest-risk servers

<!--
These are the credibility builders. Deliver them fast,
publicise the wins, and use them to secure ongoing investment.
Quick Win #2 (idle VMs) often pays for the CCoE team in month 1.
-->

---

## Phase 1: Guardrails (Weeks 5-10)

**Azure Landing Zone**
- Management group hierarchy aligned to business units
- Separate subscriptions for cost isolation and blast radius
- Azure Blueprints for repeatable deployment

**Security**
- PIM + Conditional Access baseline (massive win, zero dev friction)
- Managed Identities replacing service accounts
- NCSC CSP aligned Azure Policy initiatives

**Bare Metal Governance**
- Asset registry, patch SLAs, decommission process
- Integrate monitoring with central Log Analytics

<!--
The landing zone is the technical foundation.
PIM + Conditional Access is the single biggest security improvement
with zero developer friction — do this early and publicise it.
-->

---

## Phase 2: Enablement (Weeks 11-16)

**IaC Standards**
- Bicep (Azure), Terraform (AWS), Ansible (bare metal)
- Template library: pre-approved patterns for common workloads
- PR reviews for all infrastructure changes

**Self-Service Catalogue**
- "Deploy a web app" (App Service + SQL + WAF)
- "Deploy containers" (AKS + ACR + App Gateway)
- "Dev/test environment" (sandbox subscription)
- "Connect on-premises" (ExpressRoute + private endpoints)

**Training**
- "Cloud 101" workshop — hands-on, free sandbox
- Certification targets: AZ-900 (80% staff), AZ-104 (50%), AZ-305 (architects)

<!--
Make the right thing the easy thing.
If teams can deploy a web app in 5 minutes via the catalogue,
they'll use it instead of building from scratch.
-->

---

## Phase 3: Optimisation (Weeks 17-24)

**FinOps**
- Cost allocation tags enforced across all subscriptions
- Reserved instances / savings plans (1-year and 3-year)
- Auto-shutdown for dev/test environments
- Cost-per-workload dashboard per business unit

**Security Hardening**
- Zero Trust architecture
- Defender for Cloud on all subscriptions
- Key Vault migration — eliminate hardcoded secrets
- Automated compliance reporting (NCSC CSP)

**Bare Metal Modernisation**
- Waves: stabilise → automate → assess → migrate

<!--
By month 6, the CCoE shifts from building to optimising.
FinOps should show measurable savings by month 4.
Bare metal modernisation is a 9-12 month journey — start the assessment now.
-->

---

## Key KPIs

| Category | Metric | Month 6 | Month 12 |
|----------|--------|---------|----------|
| **Cost** | Reserved instance coverage | 40% | 70% |
| **Security** | Resources compliant with Policy | 80% | 95% |
| **Security** | Privileged access via PIM | 100% | 100% |
| **Adoption** | New deployments via IaC | 50% | 90% |
| **Adoption** | Staff certified (AZ-900+) | 30% | 80% |
| **Bare Metal** | Servers with monitoring | 50% | 100% |

<!--
Measure what matters. These KPIs show executive progress
and keep the CCoE accountable. Review monthly with leadership.
-->

